# Configuration

Settings come from flags and environment variables. Flags win; an empty or
blank variable uses the default. The program doesn't load `.env` files;
`.env.example` lists every variable.

| Flag | Variable | Default | Validation |
|---|---|---|---|
| `--tasks FILE` | `{{env_prefix}}_TASKS` | empty: the built-in sample | Readable JSON array of `{id, title, status, notes}`; ids unique, titles non-empty, status `todo`, `doing` or `done` |
| `--log-file FILE` | `{{env_prefix}}_LOG_FILE` | empty: no logs | Its directory must exist; the file is created with mode 0600 and appended to |
| `--log-level LEVEL` | `{{env_prefix}}_LOG_LEVEL` | `info` | `debug`, `info`, `warn` or `error` |
| `--no-tui` | | off | Print the tasks as text and exit |
| `--json` | | off | Print `{"tasks": [...]}` and exit; errors become `{"error": {...}}` on stderr |
| `--version` | | | Print the version (JSON with `--json`) |
| `--help` | | | Print usage |

`NO_COLOR` (any value) turns colors off in the UI; Bubble Tea's renderer
handles it, as it does the terminal's color profile.

## Exit status

| Status | When |
|---|---|
| 0 | Success, including `--help` and `--version` |
| 1 | Config, data, I/O or internal failure, including a load failure shown in the UI |
| 2 | Bad flags or arguments |
| 130 | Interrupted by a signal while the UI ran |

Every failure prints its code, the message and a `Suggestion:` line on stderr.

## Adding a setting

Give it a flag in `internal/config` with the environment variable as its
default, validate it in `Load`, and add a row to `TestLoadPrecedence`, this
file, the README table and `.env.example`.
